      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested** — Please address the inline comments regarding redundant member state across stacked CLs, boundary test coverage for `0 ms` detach timeout, and the commit message.\n\n### Review Summary\n* **Functionality:** `RtsUsbDevice::FindDfuInterface()` locates the USB DFU interface (`class \u003d 0xFE`, `subclass \u003d 0x01`) and parses its `wTransferSize`, and `RtsUsbDevice::DfuDetach()` validates the 16-bit timeout, claims the interface via `InterfaceClaim`, and sends the `DFU_DETACH` control transfer.\n* **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit:** Now that `FindDfuInterface()` returns `std::expected\u003cDfuInterfaceInfo, RtsError\u003e` by value, keeping `dfu_interface_`, `transfer_size_`, and `transfer_size()` on `RtsUsbDevice` (and resetting them in `Release()`) introduces temporary member state in this CL that is immediately deleted in the child CL (`https://crrev.com/c/8629987`). Please omit `dfu_interface_`, `transfer_size_`, and `transfer_size()` in this CL and pass `info-\u003enumber` directly in `DfuDetach()`.\n* **Code Simplicity:** Removing `dfu_interface_` and `transfer_size_` from `RtsUsbDevice` eliminates the state assignments in `DfuDetach()` and keeps `RtsUsbDevice::Release()` as a single `backend_-\u003eClose()` call.\n* **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:** Clean use of C++23 `std::expected`, `std::ranges::find_if`, `std::chrono::milliseconds`, and RAII interface claiming. In `RtsUsbDeviceDfuTest`, prefer deriving the 16-bit timeout boundary values from `UINT16_MAX` rather than raw `65535` / `65536` literals.\n* **Security:** Proper bounds checking on the 16-bit `wValue` timeout and safe descriptor handling.\n* **Testing:** Good unit test coverage of error and claim/release paths in `RtsUsbDeviceDfuTest`, but the lower valid boundary `detach_timeout \u003d\u003d 0 ms` (`std::chrono::milliseconds::zero()`) is not tested (so mutating `\u003c` to `\u003c\u003d` on line 182 of `rts5817_usb_device.cc` would not be caught).\n* **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** `Size: L (+298, -2)` (+144, -1 production lines across `rts5817_usb_device.h` and `rts5817_usb_device.cc`; +154, -1 unit test lines in `rts5817_usb_device_test.cc`). The production diff is well under 250 lines and implements a single cohesive logical change pushed into `Size: L` by its unit tests.\n* **Commit Message:** The second paragraph of `/COMMIT_MSG` still references the pre-rename `dfu_detach()` identifier and describes recording `transfer_size` on `RtsUsbDevice`.\n\n[[trajectory](https://goto.corp.google.com/traj/e0d899bb-ac40-40a8-a839-93b60aee117f)]",
